---
import StudioLayout from '../../../layouts/StudioLayout.astro';
---

<StudioLayout
  title="Career help"
  description="Private guide to Studio Career contacts."
  heading="Career help"
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-xl px-4 py-5 md:py-8">
    <p class="text-sm">
      <a href="/studio/help" class="text-gel underline-offset-2 hover:text-gold hover:underline">
        ← All help
      </a>
      {' · '}
      <a href="/studio/career" class="text-gel underline-offset-2 hover:text-gold hover:underline">
        Open Career
      </a>
    </p>

    <section class="mt-8 space-y-4">
      <h2 class="font-display text-3xl text-spotlight">Agents and casting</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-muted">
        Career contacts live in People. Each agent shows last submission, last booking (title and
        year), recency, warmth, and next step — not a dollar total unless a real invoice exists.
        Casting contacts store the last materials request the same way.
      </p>
      <ol class="list-decimal space-y-2 pl-5 text-sm text-muted">
        <li>Open <a href="/studio/career" class="text-gel hover:text-gold">Career</a>, then Agents or Casting.</li>
        <li>Open a person to edit warmth and last-touch dates. Recency is calculated from that date.</li>
        <li>
          Stale agents (default: no touch in 90 days) appear as tasks on{' '}
          <a href="/studio/career" class="text-gel hover:text-gold">Career</a> — open the person to
          log a submission or update last touch. Studio does not email agents automatically.
        </li>
      </ol>
    </section>
  </article>
</StudioLayout>
